SOLR-9490: Fixed bugs in BoolField that caused it to
 erroneously return "false" for all docs depending on usage

Here is the root cause:
The bug in `BoolField` was caused by incorrect logic in the `toExternal` method, which failed to properly handle cases where both `binaryValue()` and `stringValue()` were `null`, leading to erroneous returns of "false" for all documents. The method did not account for the possibility of returning a valid string representation when only one of the values was present, resulting in incorrect behavior when querying documents.

